## JSON Parser
## Author: Hugh Cumper
## Date Created: 16 Nov 2026
##
## A JSON parser in SSB 2.8.0, with a tree and typed accessor functions.
##
## json_load (file) and json_parse (string) replace ONE current document.
## Check jsonDoc.error% before using root%; navigate with json_member%, json_at%
## or sibling links. json_name$ returns an object member's decoded name.
## json_clear clears accessor errors (8/9); json_free releases the arrays.
##
## Storage: jsonChunks$ holds source bytes in 512-byte strings; jsonNodes holds
## one record per value with source spans; jsonFrames holds unfinished containers.
## Strings decode on demand; numbers retain their spelling until conversion.
##
## Each node uses 32 bytes of fields: 8000 nodes need about 256 KB, 32766 about
## 1 MB, plus input and array overhead. Arrays retain their largest bounds until
## json_free. A failed DIM is a BASIC runtime error. TURBO_objdat must cover the
## arrays; with TURBO_windo 0, running out of dataspace stops the program.
##
## Target: SMSQ/E SBASIC or Turbo. Integer FOR counters and SELect ON are not
## supported correctly by the original Sinclair JS/MG interpreters.
##
## Handles are signed integers 1..capacity; zero means no link/missing member.
## JSON null has kind% 7. Array indices are zero-based; source positions are
## one-based. Positions/lengths have no % suffix to allow files beyond 32767 bytes.
## The global document is not reentrant. Loading again invalidates old handles,
## even if their indices remain in range. Treat parsed records/chunks as read-only.
## UTF-8 remains bytes; no conversion to the QL display character set is performed.
##
## Document position is the next byte (bytes+1 at EOF); used% includes partial
## trees on failure, but failed loads/parses set root% to zero. The first error
## is retained; tokenStart/tokenLength are temporary string-scan results.
TYPE JsonDocument
  bytes
  position
  capacity%
  used%
  root%
  depth%
  maxDepth%
  error%
  errorPosition
  errorLine
  errorColumn
  message$(160)
  tokenStart
  tokenLength
END TYPE

## Tree node kinds: 1 object, 2 array, 3 string, 4 number, 5 true, 6 false, 7 null.
## first% links the first child; next% links siblings. Scalars have count% zero.
## Object children are VALUES with attached names: {"a":1,"b":2} uses three nodes.
## start/length span the whole value, including quotes/brackets. keyStart/keyLength
## span the name WITHOUT quotes, retaining escapes. keyStart = 0 means no name;
## an empty name has nonzero keyStart and zero keyLength.
## Children are links, not embedded records; copying a node is not a deep copy.
TYPE JsonNode
  kind%
  first%
  next%
  count%
  start
  length
  keyStart
  keyLength
END TYPE

## One frame per unfinished container; node% identifies it and last% allows
## constant-time append in source order. phase% controls the next legal token:
## 0: first item or close; 1: item required after comma; 2: comma or close.
## Separating phases 0 and 1 rejects trailing commas.
## Save object key spans here before reading the value: a string value overwrites
## the document's temporary token span.
TYPE JsonFrame
  node%
  phase%
  last%
  keyStart
  keyLength
END TYPE

## Declare storage/ranks before use. Zero-bound placeholders grow on demand.
## jsonArena%, jsonStack% and jsonSlots% track allocated bounds for later reuse.
## Slot zero is never a value handle. Nodes are allocated per document, without
## individual frees or a POOL allocator that would STOP on exhaustion.
DIM jsonDoc AS JsonDocument
DIM jsonNodes(0) AS JsonNode
DIM jsonFrames(0) AS JsonFrame
DIM jsonChunks$(0,512)
jsonArena% = 0 : jsonStack% = 0 : jsonSlots% = 0

## INTERNAL: invalidate the old document, check limits, and size the arena.
## Record declarations reset fields; clearing the document first prevents a bad
## configuration from exposing the previous root. Limits protect signed handles
## and bound container depth/input size; insufficient RAM still raises a DIM error.
## SSB expands record-array DIM into one DIM and clearing loop per field.
## Grow arrays only when needed; json_value% clears each reused node on allocation
## so old links cannot enter the new tree.
## The chunk bound includes an unused final slot for exact multiples of 512,
## and the same allocation formula also handles empty input.
DEFine PROCedure json_begin(VAL jbBytes, VAL jbCapacity%, VAL jbDepth%)
  LOCal jbChunk%,jbSlots%
  DIM jsonDoc AS JsonDocument
  jsonDoc.position = 1
  IF jbBytes < 0 OR jbBytes > 1048576 THEN
    json_fail 1,"Input limit is 1048576 bytes"
    RETurn
  END IF
  IF jbCapacity% < 1 OR jbCapacity% > 32766 THEN
    json_fail 1,"Node capacity must be 1..32766"
    RETurn
  END IF
  IF jbDepth% < 1 OR jbDepth% > 256 THEN
    json_fail 1,"Depth limit must be 1..256"
    RETurn
  END IF
  jsonDoc.bytes = jbBytes
  jsonDoc.capacity% = jbCapacity%
  jsonDoc.maxDepth% = jbDepth%
  IF jbCapacity% > jsonArena% THEN
    DIM jsonNodes(jbCapacity%) AS JsonNode
    jsonArena% = jbCapacity%
  END IF
  IF jbDepth% > jsonStack% THEN
    DIM jsonFrames(jbDepth%) AS JsonFrame
    jsonStack% = jbDepth%
  END IF
  jbSlots% = INT(jbBytes/512)
  IF jbSlots% > jsonSlots% THEN
    DIM jsonChunks$(jbSlots%,512)
    jsonSlots% = jbSlots%
  END IF
  ## Turbo may reuse string-array contents on DIM, and reused chunks hold the
  ## previous document. Clear the slots this document uses before loading it.
  FOR jbChunk% = 0 TO jbSlots%
    jsonChunks$(jbChunk%) = ""
  END FOR jbChunk%
END DEFine

## PUBLIC: shrink every array back to its placeholder and forget the document.
## Old handles become invalid; the next load or parse allocates again.
DEFine PROCedure json_free
  DIM jsonDoc AS JsonDocument
  DIM jsonNodes(0) AS JsonNode
  DIM jsonFrames(0) AS JsonFrame
  DIM jsonChunks$(0,512)
  jsonArena% = 0 : jsonStack% = 0 : jsonSlots% = 0
END DEFine

## PUBLIC: json_load file$, nodeCapacity%, maxFileBytes, maxContainerDepth%.
## Validate configuration before opening. FOP_IN chooses a free channel or returns
## a negative QDOS error; FLEN supplies the input size for the second json_begin.
## The node arena is reused, so only additional chunk storage may be needed.
## Read exactly FLEN bytes, preserving line endings and byte offsets. INKEY$ uses
## timeout -1: zero-timeout reads can return nothing while a drive fetches a block.
## EOF returns "", reported as error 2 if fewer than FLEN bytes have been read.
## Fill chunks with spaces, then store bytes in place to avoid repeated copying.
## On short read, trim the chunk so json_byte% still returns -1 for missing bytes.
## Close the input-only channel on each normal return after opening.
## Unexpected OS I/O exceptions remain BASIC runtime errors.
## Parse only a complete load; failures never publish a partial root.
DEFine PROCedure json_load(VAL jlFile$, VAL jlCapacity%, VAL jlMaxBytes, VAL jlDepth%)
  LOCal jlChannel%,jlSize,jlPosition,jlChunk%,jlOffset%,jlFill,jlByte$(1)
  json_begin 0,jlCapacity%,jlDepth%
  IF jsonDoc.error% THEN RETurn
  IF jlMaxBytes < 0 OR jlMaxBytes > 1048576 THEN
    json_fail 1,"File byte limit must be 0..1048576"
    RETurn
  END IF
  jlChannel% = FOP_IN(jlFile$)
  IF jlChannel% < 0 THEN
    json_fail 2,"Cannot open JSON file"
    RETurn
  END IF
  jlSize = FLEN(#jlChannel%)
  IF jlSize > jlMaxBytes OR jlSize < 0 THEN
    CLOSE #jlChannel%
    json_fail 1,"JSON file exceeds byte limit"
    RETurn
  END IF
  json_begin jlSize,jlCapacity%,jlDepth%
  IF jsonDoc.error% THEN CLOSE #jlChannel% : RETurn
  FOR jlPosition = 1 TO jlSize
    jlChunk% = INT((jlPosition-1)/512) : jlOffset% = jlPosition-512*jlChunk%
    IF jlOffset% = 1 THEN
      jlFill = jlSize-jlPosition+1 : IF jlFill > 512 THEN jlFill = 512
      jsonChunks$(jlChunk%) = FILL$(" ",jlFill)
    END IF
    jlByte$ = INKEY$(#jlChannel%,-1)
    IF LEN(jlByte$) <> 1 THEN
      IF jlOffset% = 1 THEN
        jsonChunks$(jlChunk%) = ""
      ELSE
        jsonChunks$(jlChunk%) = jsonChunks$(jlChunk%,1 TO jlOffset%-1)
      END IF
      jsonDoc.position = jlPosition
      json_fail 2,"Unexpected end while reading JSON file"
      EXIT jlPosition
    END IF
    jsonChunks$(jlChunk%,jlOffset%) = jlByte$
  END FOR jlPosition
  CLOSE #jlChannel%
  IF NOT jsonDoc.error% THEN json_read
END DEFine

## PUBLIC: parse an existing string, with json_load's tree/error contract.
## This entry point inherits the QL single-string limit; file input does not.
## Both populate the same chunks. VAL gives scalar arguments value semantics;
## distinct local prefixes avoid interference through S*BASIC's dynamic scope.
DEFine PROCedure json_parse(VAL jpText$, VAL jpCapacity%, VAL jpDepth%)
  LOCal jpPosition,jpChunk%,jpAmount%
  json_begin LEN(jpText$),jpCapacity%,jpDepth%
  IF jsonDoc.error% THEN RETurn
  jpPosition = 1 : jpChunk% = 0
  REPeat jpCopy
    IF jpPosition > LEN(jpText$) THEN EXIT jpCopy
    jpAmount% = LEN(jpText$)-jpPosition+1
    IF jpAmount% > 512 THEN jpAmount% = 512
    jsonChunks$(jpChunk%) = jpText$(jpPosition TO jpPosition+jpAmount%-1)
    jpPosition = jpPosition+jpAmount% : jpChunk% = jpChunk%+1
  END REPeat jpCopy
  json_read
END DEFine

## INTERNAL: map absolute bytes to chunks: byte 1 = chunk 0/character 1;
## byte 513 = chunk 1/character 1. Return -1 outside the input or loaded chunk.
## The sentinel differs from NUL (0), preventing embedded NUL from acting as EOF.
## The loaded-length check also supports short-read diagnostics.
DEFine FuNction json_byte%(VAL jcPosition)
  LOCal jcChunk%,jcOffset%
  IF jcPosition < 1 OR jcPosition > jsonDoc.bytes THEN RETurn -1
  jcChunk% = INT((jcPosition-1)/512)
  jcOffset% = jcPosition-512*jcChunk%
  IF jcOffset% > LEN(jsonChunks$(jcChunk%)) THEN RETurn -1
  RETurn CODE(jsonChunks$(jcChunk%,jcOffset%))
END DEFine

## INTERNAL: latch the first error; later failures must not hide its cause.
## json_valid% blocks accessors while an error is set. json_fail uses the parser
## cursor; json_failat lets accessors report the affected node/span instead.
## Scan the prefix only on failure for one-based line/byte-column; CRLF counts
## as one line ending, and isolated CR/LF also start new lines.
## Classes: 1 config/byte limit, 2 file, 3 structure, 4 string/Unicode, 5 number
## syntax, 6 node capacity, 7 depth, 8 accessor misuse, 9 getter/conversion limit.
## Zero results alone do not mean success. json_clear can reset classes 8/9.
DEFine PROCedure json_fail(VAL jfCode%, VAL jfMessage$)
  json_failat jfCode%,jsonDoc.position,jfMessage$
END DEFine

DEFine PROCedure json_failat(VAL joCode%, VAL joAt, VAL joMessage$)
  LOCal joPosition,joByte%,joCR%
  IF jsonDoc.error% THEN RETurn
  jsonDoc.error% = joCode% : jsonDoc.message$ = joMessage$
  jsonDoc.errorPosition = joAt
  jsonDoc.errorLine = 1 : jsonDoc.errorColumn = 1 : joCR% = 0
  FOR joPosition = 1 TO joAt-1
    joByte% = json_byte%(joPosition)
    IF joByte% = 13 THEN
      jsonDoc.errorLine = jsonDoc.errorLine+1
      jsonDoc.errorColumn = 1 : joCR% = 1
    ELSE
      IF joByte% = 10 THEN
        IF NOT joCR% THEN jsonDoc.errorLine = jsonDoc.errorLine+1
        jsonDoc.errorColumn = 1
      ELSE
        jsonDoc.errorColumn = jsonDoc.errorColumn+1
      END IF
      joCR% = 0
    END IF
  END FOR joPosition
END DEFine

## PUBLIC: forget an accessor error (class 8 or 9) after a successful parse, so
## the caller can keep using the same document. Load, parse, capacity and depth
## errors (classes 1 to 7) stay set: their documents have no usable root.
DEFine PROCedure json_clear
  IF jsonDoc.error% < 8 THEN RETurn
  jsonDoc.error% = 0 : jsonDoc.message$ = ""
  jsonDoc.errorPosition = 0 : jsonDoc.errorLine = 0 : jsonDoc.errorColumn = 0
END DEFine

## INTERNAL: consume only JSON whitespace: space, tab, LF and CR.
## Do not accept every character a BASIC trim function might treat as blank.
## EOF (-1) and every other byte are left for the grammar to interpret.
DEFine PROCedure json_space
  LOCal jwByte%
  REPeat jwSkip
    jwByte% = json_byte%(jsonDoc.position)
    IF jwByte% <> 32 AND jwByte% <> 9 AND jwByte% <> 10 AND jwByte% <> 13 THEN EXIT jwSkip
    jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
  END REPeat jwSkip
END DEFine

## INTERNAL ASCII digit predicate. Locale-specific digit characters are not
## JSON number digits. The EOF sentinel naturally returns false as well.
DEFine FuNction json_digit%(VAL jdByte%)
  RETurn jdByte% >= 48 AND jdByte% <= 57
END DEFine

## INTERNAL: read four hex digits at jhPosition; accept either letter case.
## Success leaves the cursor unchanged; the caller consumes the escape.
## On failure, move to the bad/missing digit before recording the string error.
## Result 0..65535 is a Unicode code unit, too wide for a signed %-suffixed value.
DEFine FuNction json_hex4(VAL jhPosition)
  LOCal jhIndex%,jhByte%,jhDigit%,jhValue
  jhValue = 0
  FOR jhIndex% = 0 TO 3
    jhByte% = json_byte%(jhPosition+jhIndex%) : jhDigit% = -1
    IF jhByte% >= 48 AND jhByte% <= 57 THEN jhDigit% = jhByte%-48
    IF jhByte% >= 65 AND jhByte% <= 70 THEN jhDigit% = jhByte%-55
    IF jhByte% >= 97 AND jhByte% <= 102 THEN jhDigit% = jhByte%-87
    IF jhDigit% < 0 THEN
      jsonDoc.position = jhPosition+jhIndex%
      json_fail 4,"Expected four hexadecimal escape digits"
      RETurn 0
    END IF
    jhValue = jhValue*16+jhDigit%
  END FOR jhIndex%
  RETurn jhValue
END DEFine

## INTERNAL: validate a literal non-ASCII scalar; return its length (2..4 bytes).
## The lead byte gives length/payload; each continuation contributes six bits.
## Reject stray continuations, C0/C1 prefixes, incomplete/overlong encodings,
## surrogate scalars and values above U+10FFFF.
## Original bytes remain unchanged, without normalization.
## The string scanner handles ASCII itself.
DEFine FuNction json_utf8size%(VAL juPosition)
  LOCal juByte%,juLength%,juIndex%,juNext%,juCode
  juByte% = json_byte%(juPosition) : juLength% = 0 : juCode = 0
  IF juByte% >= 194 AND juByte% <= 223 THEN juLength% = 2 : juCode = juByte%-192
  IF juByte% >= 224 AND juByte% <= 239 THEN juLength% = 3 : juCode = juByte%-224
  IF juByte% >= 240 AND juByte% <= 244 THEN juLength% = 4 : juCode = juByte%-240
  IF juLength% = 0 THEN json_fail 4,"Invalid UTF-8 leading byte" : RETurn 0
  FOR juIndex% = 1 TO juLength%-1
    juNext% = json_byte%(juPosition+juIndex%)
    IF juNext% < 128 OR juNext% > 191 THEN
      jsonDoc.position = juPosition+juIndex%
      json_fail 4,"Invalid UTF-8 continuation byte"
      RETurn 0
    END IF
    juCode = juCode*64+juNext%-128
  END FOR juIndex%
  IF (juLength% = 3 AND juCode < 2048) OR (juLength% = 4 AND juCode < 65536) THEN
    json_fail 4,"Overlong UTF-8 sequence" : RETurn 0
  END IF
  IF juCode > 1114111 OR (juCode >= 55296 AND juCode <= 57343) THEN
    json_fail 4,"Invalid Unicode scalar" : RETurn 0
  END IF
  RETurn juLength%
END DEFine

## INTERNAL string lexer: enter at the opening quote; finish just after closing.
## tokenStart/tokenLength span the contents, without building a decoded string.
## Long tokens can therefore parse even when a getter cannot return them whole.
## Validate simple escapes and four-hex-digit Unicode escapes. High surrogates
## require an immediate low-surrogate escape; isolated low surrogates are invalid.
## Reject unescaped control bytes and EOF (-1). Escaped quotes cannot close strings.
## This library requires Unicode scalars, rejecting malformed UTF-16 escapes.
DEFine PROCedure json_scanstring
  LOCal jsByte%,jsEscape%,jsLength%,jsUnit,jsLow
  jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
  jsonDoc.tokenStart = jsonDoc.position
  REPeat jsScan
    jsByte% = json_byte%(jsonDoc.position)
    IF jsByte% = 34 THEN
      jsonDoc.tokenLength = jsonDoc.position-jsonDoc.tokenStart
      jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
      RETurn
    END IF
    IF jsByte% < 32 THEN json_fail 4,"Unterminated string or unescaped control byte" : RETurn
    IF jsByte% = 92 THEN
      jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
      jsEscape% = json_byte%(jsonDoc.position)
      IF jsEscape% = 117 THEN
        jsUnit = json_hex4(jsonDoc.position+1)
        IF jsonDoc.error% THEN RETurn
        jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+5
        IF jsUnit >= 55296 AND jsUnit <= 56319 THEN
          IF json_byte%(jsonDoc.position) <> 92 OR json_byte%(jsonDoc.position+1) <> 117 THEN
            json_fail 4,"High surrogate requires a low surrogate escape" : RETurn
          END IF
          jsLow = json_hex4(jsonDoc.position+2)
          IF jsonDoc.error% THEN RETurn
          IF jsLow < 56320 OR jsLow > 57343 THEN json_fail 4,"Invalid low surrogate" : RETurn
          jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+6
        ELSE
          IF jsUnit >= 56320 AND jsUnit <= 57343 THEN json_fail 4,"Unpaired low surrogate" : RETurn
        END IF
      ELSE
        IF jsEscape% <> 34 AND jsEscape% <> 92 AND jsEscape% <> 47 AND jsEscape% <> 98 AND jsEscape% <> 102 AND jsEscape% <> 110 AND jsEscape% <> 114 AND jsEscape% <> 116 THEN
          json_fail 4,"Invalid JSON string escape" : RETurn
        END IF
        jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
      END IF
    ELSE
      jsLength% = 1
      IF jsByte% >= 128 THEN jsLength% = json_utf8size%(jsonDoc.position)
      IF jsonDoc.error% THEN RETurn
      jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+jsLength%
    END IF
  END REPeat jsScan
END DEFine

## INTERNAL number lexer: optional minus, zero or nonzero-leading integer,
## optional fraction with digits, optional exponent with optional sign and digits.
## After a leading zero, leave further digits for the outer grammar to reject.
## Finish at the first byte after the token, without converting it. Huge exponents
## remain valid JSON; json_number applies QL conversion limits later.
DEFine PROCedure json_scannumber
  LOCal jnByte%
  IF json_byte%(jsonDoc.position) = 45 THEN jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
  jnByte% = json_byte%(jsonDoc.position)
  IF jnByte% = 48 THEN
    jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
  ELSE
    IF jnByte% < 49 OR jnByte% > 57 THEN json_fail 5,"Expected integer digits" : RETurn
    REPeat jnInteger
      jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
      IF NOT json_digit%(json_byte%(jsonDoc.position)) THEN EXIT jnInteger
    END REPeat jnInteger
  END IF
  IF json_byte%(jsonDoc.position) = 46 THEN
    jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
    IF NOT json_digit%(json_byte%(jsonDoc.position)) THEN json_fail 5,"Fraction requires digits" : RETurn
    REPeat jnFraction
      jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
      IF NOT json_digit%(json_byte%(jsonDoc.position)) THEN EXIT jnFraction
    END REPeat jnFraction
  END IF
  jnByte% = json_byte%(jsonDoc.position)
  IF jnByte% = 69 OR jnByte% = 101 THEN
    jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
    jnByte% = json_byte%(jsonDoc.position)
    IF jnByte% = 43 OR jnByte% = 45 THEN jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
    IF NOT json_digit%(json_byte%(jsonDoc.position)) THEN json_fail 5,"Exponent requires digits" : RETurn
    REPeat jnExponent
      jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
      IF NOT json_digit%(json_byte%(jsonDoc.position)) THEN EXIT jnExponent
    END REPeat jnExponent
  END IF
END DEFine

## INTERNAL: consume the exact lowercase bytes of true, false, or null.
## The enclosing grammar checks the following delimiter, so truex is rejected
## even though this routine has successfully consumed its true prefix.
DEFine PROCedure json_literal(VAL jtText$)
  LOCal jtIndex%
  FOR jtIndex% = 1 TO LEN(jtText$)
    IF json_byte%(jsonDoc.position) <> CODE(jtText$(jtIndex%)) THEN
      json_fail 3,"Invalid JSON literal" : RETurn
    END IF
    jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
  END FOR jtIndex%
END DEFine

## INTERNAL: allocate a value in source/preorder and return its handle, or zero
## with error% set. Links describe the tree; children need not be contiguous.
## Clear every field of reused slots to remove earlier links, counts and key spans.
## Consume scalars fully; for {/[ consume only the opening byte, leaving children
## to json_read's explicit stack. Container lengths are finalized on closing.
## Failure may leave allocated slots, but root% = 0 hides the partial tree.
## The next load/parse resets document state and reuses the arena.
DEFine FuNction json_value%
  LOCal jvNode%,jvByte%
  json_space
  IF jsonDoc.used% >= jsonDoc.capacity% THEN json_fail 6,"JSON node capacity exhausted" : RETurn 0
  jsonDoc.used% = jsonDoc.used%+1 : jvNode% = jsonDoc.used%
  jsonNodes(jvNode%).kind% = 0 : jsonNodes(jvNode%).first% = 0
  jsonNodes(jvNode%).next% = 0 : jsonNodes(jvNode%).count% = 0
  jsonNodes(jvNode%).length = 0 : jsonNodes(jvNode%).keyStart = 0
  jsonNodes(jvNode%).keyLength = 0
  jsonNodes(jvNode%).start = jsonDoc.position
  jvByte% = json_byte%(jsonDoc.position)
  SELect ON jvByte%
    ON jvByte% = 123
      jsonNodes(jvNode%).kind% = 1 : jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
    ON jvByte% = 91
      jsonNodes(jvNode%).kind% = 2 : jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
    ON jvByte% = 34
      jsonNodes(jvNode%).kind% = 3 : json_scanstring
    ON jvByte% = 116
      jsonNodes(jvNode%).kind% = 5 : json_literal "true"
    ON jvByte% = 102
      jsonNodes(jvNode%).kind% = 6 : json_literal "false"
    ON jvByte% = 110
      jsonNodes(jvNode%).kind% = 7 : json_literal "null"
    ON jvByte% = REMAINDER
      IF jvByte% = 45 OR json_digit%(jvByte%) THEN
        jsonNodes(jvNode%).kind% = 4 : json_scannumber
      ELSE
        json_fail 3,"Expected a JSON value"
      END IF
  END SELect
  IF jsonDoc.error% THEN RETurn 0
  jsonNodes(jvNode%).length = jsonDoc.position-jsonNodes(jvNode%).start
  RETurn jvNode%
END DEFine

## INTERNAL: descend into a newly opened object or array.
## Only containers use stack entries, so a scalar root needs no frame. Check the
## depth limit BEFORE indexing the stack; reaching it is an ordinary parser error.
## Reused frames reset phase/last, while key spans are overwritten before use.
DEFine PROCedure json_push(VAL jkNode%)
  LOCal jkDepth%
  IF jsonDoc.depth% >= jsonDoc.maxDepth% THEN json_fail 7,"JSON nesting limit exceeded" : RETurn
  jsonDoc.depth% = jsonDoc.depth%+1 : jkDepth% = jsonDoc.depth%
  jsonFrames(jkDepth%).node% = jkNode%
  jsonFrames(jkDepth%).phase% = 0 : jsonFrames(jkDepth%).last% = 0
END DEFine

## INTERNAL iterative grammar driver: parse one root and its nested containers,
## then require whitespace to EOF. Accept a UTF-8 BOM only at the document start.
## Inspect the top frame: close it, consume a comma, or read the next item.
## Object items are name/colon/value; array items are values. Link each new child
## to first/next, increment the direct-child count, and mark the parent waiting
## for comma/end BEFORE pushing a child container, preserving its continuation.
## jrFrame% saves the parent index; copy the key span before the stack can grow.
## The closing byte must match the parent's kind, so } cannot close an array.
## Each successful iteration advances input or pops a frame. Nesting uses the
## explicit stack rather than proportional BASIC procedure recursion.
DEFine PROCedure json_read
  LOCal jrFrame%,jrParent%,jrKind%,jrByte%,jrChild%,jrLast%,jrClose%,jrPhase%
  ## Permit a UTF-8 BOM only at the start of a document.
  IF json_byte%(1) = 239 AND json_byte%(2) = 187 AND json_byte%(3) = 191 THEN jsonDoc.position = 4
  jsonDoc.root% = json_value%
  IF jsonDoc.error% THEN jsonDoc.root% = 0 : RETurn
  jrParent% = jsonDoc.root%
  IF jsonNodes(jrParent%).kind% <= 2 THEN json_push jrParent%
  REPeat jrParse
    IF jsonDoc.error% OR jsonDoc.depth% = 0 THEN EXIT jrParse
    jrFrame% = jsonDoc.depth% : jrParent% = jsonFrames(jrFrame%).node%
    jrKind% = jsonNodes(jrParent%).kind% : jrPhase% = jsonFrames(jrFrame%).phase%
    jrClose% = 93 : IF jrKind% = 1 THEN jrClose% = 125
    json_space : jrByte% = json_byte%(jsonDoc.position)
## A close is legal for an empty container (phase 0) or after an item
## (phase 2), but never immediately after a comma (phase 1).
    IF jrByte% = jrClose% AND jrPhase% <> 1 THEN
      jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
      jsonNodes(jrParent%).length = jsonDoc.position-jsonNodes(jrParent%).start
      jsonDoc.depth% = jsonDoc.depth%-1
    ELSE
      IF jrPhase% = 2 THEN
        IF jrByte% <> 44 THEN json_fail 3,"Expected comma or container end" : EXIT jrParse
        jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1 : jsonFrames(jrFrame%).phase% = 1
      ELSE
        IF jrKind% = 1 THEN
          IF jrByte% <> 34 THEN json_fail 3,"Expected an object member name" : EXIT jrParse
          json_scanstring
          IF jsonDoc.error% THEN EXIT jrParse
          jsonFrames(jrFrame%).keyStart = jsonDoc.tokenStart
          jsonFrames(jrFrame%).keyLength = jsonDoc.tokenLength
          json_space
          IF json_byte%(jsonDoc.position) <> 58 THEN json_fail 3,"Expected colon after member name" : EXIT jrParse
          jsonDoc.position = jsonDoc.position+1
        END IF
        jrChild% = json_value%
        IF jsonDoc.error% THEN EXIT jrParse
        IF jrKind% = 1 THEN
          jsonNodes(jrChild%).keyStart = jsonFrames(jrFrame%).keyStart
          jsonNodes(jrChild%).keyLength = jsonFrames(jrFrame%).keyLength
        END IF
        jrLast% = jsonFrames(jrFrame%).last%
## Only the previous LAST direct child's next% is changed. That child's own
## children form a separate chain and are not part of the sibling traversal.
        IF jrLast% = 0 THEN
          jsonNodes(jrParent%).first% = jrChild%
        ELSE
          jsonNodes(jrLast%).next% = jrChild%
        END IF
        jsonFrames(jrFrame%).last% = jrChild% : jsonFrames(jrFrame%).phase% = 2
        jsonNodes(jrParent%).count% = jsonNodes(jrParent%).count%+1
        IF jsonNodes(jrChild%).kind% <= 2 THEN json_push jrChild%
      END IF
    END IF
  END REPeat jrParse
  IF NOT jsonDoc.error% THEN
    json_space
    IF jsonDoc.position <= jsonDoc.bytes THEN json_fail 3,"Unexpected text after JSON value"
  END IF
  IF jsonDoc.error% THEN jsonDoc.root% = 0
END DEFine

## INTERNAL common accessor guard. A latched parse/accessor error blocks
## further work; otherwise check the handle's range before indexing the arena.
## This is not a generation check: a stale handle reused after another load can
## still be in range. Keeping handles across loads is the caller's error.
DEFine FuNction json_valid%(VAL jaNode%)
  IF jsonDoc.error% THEN RETurn 0
  IF jaNode% < 1 OR jaNode% > jsonDoc.used% THEN
    json_fail 8,"Invalid JSON node handle" : RETurn 0
  END IF
  RETurn 1
END DEFine

## INTERNAL exact byte comparison of decoded names: A and a are distinct.
## Compare CODEs rather than BASIC's ordinary string collation.
## No Unicode normalization: different scalar sequences remain different keys,
## even if they look identical when displayed.
DEFine FuNction json_equal%(VAL jeLeft$, VAL jeRight$)
  LOCal jeIndex%
  IF LEN(jeLeft$) <> LEN(jeRight$) THEN RETurn 0
  FOR jeIndex% = 1 TO LEN(jeLeft$)
    IF CODE(jeLeft$(jeIndex%)) <> CODE(jeRight$(jeIndex%)) THEN RETurn 0
  END FOR jeIndex%
  RETurn 1
END DEFine

## INTERNAL: compare a raw key span with a decoded name. Escapes shorten text,
## so a shorter span cannot match. Equal lengths require identical bytes without
## backslashes; compare those in place. Decode only longer spans, which would
## need escapes to match. Most ordinary lookups build no strings.
DEFine FuNction json_keyis%(VAL jiStart, VAL jiLength, VAL jiName$)
  LOCal jiIndex,jiByte%
  IF jiLength < LEN(jiName$) THEN RETurn 0
  IF jiLength > LEN(jiName$) THEN RETurn json_equal%(json_decode$(jiStart,jiLength),jiName$)
  FOR jiIndex = 1 TO jiLength
    jiByte% = json_byte%(jiStart+jiIndex-1)
    IF jiByte% = 92 OR jiByte% <> CODE(jiName$(jiIndex)) THEN RETurn 0
  END FOR jiIndex
  RETurn 1
END DEFine

## INTERNAL: encode a validated scalar as 1..4 UTF-8 bytes; the caller has
## already combined surrogate pairs. Split the payload into six-bit groups.
## Real-valued locals avoid the QL signed 16-bit limit; output is at most four bytes.
## QL display-character conversion is deliberately not implicit.
DEFine FuNction json_utf8$(VAL jyCode)
  LOCal jyOut$(4),jyLast,jyMiddle,jyUpper
  ## Turbo's MOD can coerce operands to signed integers. Use real arithmetic
  ## for Unicode scalars above 32767, including supplementary characters.
  jyLast = jyCode-64*INT(jyCode/64)
  jyMiddle = INT(jyCode/64)-64*INT(jyCode/4096)
  jyUpper = INT(jyCode/4096)-64*INT(jyCode/262144)
  IF jyCode < 128 THEN RETurn CHR$(jyCode)
  IF jyCode < 2048 THEN
    jyOut$ = CHR$(192+INT(jyCode/64)) & CHR$(128+jyLast)
    RETurn jyOut$
  END IF
  IF jyCode < 65536 THEN
    jyOut$ = CHR$(224+INT(jyCode/4096)) & CHR$(128+jyMiddle)
    RETurn jyOut$ & CHR$(128+jyLast)
  END IF
  jyOut$ = CHR$(240+INT(jyCode/262144)) & CHR$(128+jyUpper)
  RETurn jyOut$ & CHR$(128+jyMiddle) & CHR$(128+jyLast)
END DEFine

## INTERNAL: decode a validated string/key CONTENT span; its end is exclusive.
## Copy literals, replace escapes, and encode Unicode as UTF-8. Supplementary
## scalars use 65536 + (high-55296)*1024 + (low-56320).
## Assume validated chunks/spans remain unchanged. Results may contain NUL/control
## bytes: use LEN, not NUL termination.
## Check the 4096-byte OUTPUT limit before appending; escaped and decoded lengths
## can differ. Report overflow at the span's start, without silent truncation.
DEFine FuNction json_decode$(VAL jxStart, VAL jxLength)
  LOCal jxOut$(4096),jxPart$(4),jxPosition,jxEnd,jxByte%,jxEscape%,jxUnit,jxLow
  jxOut$ = "" : jxPosition = jxStart : jxEnd = jxStart+jxLength
  REPeat jxDecode
    IF jxPosition >= jxEnd OR jsonDoc.error% THEN EXIT jxDecode
    jxByte% = json_byte%(jxPosition) : jxPosition = jxPosition+1
    jxPart$ = CHR$(jxByte%)
    IF jxByte% = 92 THEN
      jxEscape% = json_byte%(jxPosition) : jxPosition = jxPosition+1
      SELect ON jxEscape%
        ON jxEscape% = 98 : jxPart$ = CHR$(8)
        ON jxEscape% = 102 : jxPart$ = CHR$(12)
        ON jxEscape% = 110 : jxPart$ = CHR$(10)
        ON jxEscape% = 114 : jxPart$ = CHR$(13)
        ON jxEscape% = 116 : jxPart$ = CHR$(9)
        ON jxEscape% = 117
          jxUnit = json_hex4(jxPosition) : jxPosition = jxPosition+4
          IF jxUnit >= 55296 AND jxUnit <= 56319 THEN
            jxLow = json_hex4(jxPosition+2) : jxPosition = jxPosition+6
            jxUnit = 65536+(jxUnit-55296)*1024+jxLow-56320
          END IF
          jxPart$ = json_utf8$(jxUnit)
        ON jxEscape% = REMAINDER : jxPart$ = CHR$(jxEscape%)
      END SELect
    END IF
    IF LEN(jxOut$)+LEN(jxPart$) > 4096 THEN json_failat 9,jxStart,"Decoded string exceeds 4096 bytes" : RETurn ""
    jxOut$ = jxOut$ & jxPart$
  END REPeat jxDecode
  RETurn jxOut$
END DEFine

## PUBLIC: search direct object children for the first exact decoded name.
## Duplicates remain ordered; a and its Unicode-escaped spelling match alike.
## json_keyis% compares raw bytes where possible, decoding longer spans as needed.
## Missing names return 0 without error; wrong node types report error 8.
## Search is linear in member count. If decoding is needed, the decoder's size
## limit applies and overflow reports error 9.
DEFine FuNction json_member%(VAL jmNode%, VAL jmName$)
  LOCal jmChild%
  IF NOT json_valid%(jmNode%) THEN RETurn 0
  IF jsonNodes(jmNode%).kind% <> 1 THEN json_failat 8,jsonNodes(jmNode%).start,"Object required" : RETurn 0
  jmChild% = jsonNodes(jmNode%).first%
  REPeat jmFind
    IF jmChild% = 0 OR jsonDoc.error% THEN EXIT jmFind
    IF json_keyis%(jsonNodes(jmChild%).keyStart,jsonNodes(jmChild%).keyLength,jmName$) THEN RETurn jmChild%
    jmChild% = jsonNodes(jmChild%).next%
  END REPeat jmFind
  RETurn 0
END DEFine

## PUBLIC: the decoded member name of a value inside an object, for callers that
## walk an object's first%/next% links instead of looking names up. A value that
## is not an object member (keyStart = 0) is accessor misuse (error 8).
DEFine FuNction json_name$(VAL jnmNode%)
  IF NOT json_valid%(jnmNode%) THEN RETurn ""
  IF jsonNodes(jnmNode%).keyStart = 0 THEN json_failat 8,jsonNodes(jnmNode%).start,"Object member required" : RETurn ""
  RETurn json_decode$(jsonNodes(jnmNode%).keyStart,jsonNodes(jnmNode%).keyLength)
END DEFine

## PUBLIC: select a zero-based array index by following next% links.
## Negative and past-the-end indices return 0 without an error; a non-array
## handle is accessor misuse (error 8). For a full traversal, start at first%
## and follow next% instead: repeatedly indexing 0,1,2,... rescans earlier items.
DEFine FuNction json_at%(VAL jaArray%, VAL jaIndex%)
  LOCal jaChild%,jaCount%
  IF NOT json_valid%(jaArray%) THEN RETurn 0
  IF jsonNodes(jaArray%).kind% <> 2 THEN json_failat 8,jsonNodes(jaArray%).start,"Array required" : RETurn 0
  IF jaIndex% < 0 THEN RETurn 0
  jaChild% = jsonNodes(jaArray%).first% : jaCount% = 0
  REPeat jaFind
    IF jaChild% = 0 OR jaCount% = jaIndex% THEN EXIT jaFind
    jaChild% = jsonNodes(jaChild%).next% : jaCount% = jaCount%+1
  END REPeat jaFind
  RETurn jaChild%
END DEFine

## PUBLIC string accessor. Node spans include their quotes; remove exactly
## one byte at each end before decoding. An empty JSON string returns "" with
## error% still zero. A wrong type also returns "" but sets error% = 8.
DEFine FuNction json_string$(VAL jgNode%)
  IF NOT json_valid%(jgNode%) THEN RETurn ""
  IF jsonNodes(jgNode%).kind% <> 3 THEN json_failat 8,jsonNodes(jgNode%).start,"String required" : RETurn ""
  RETurn json_decode$(jsonNodes(jgNode%).start+1,jsonNodes(jgNode%).length-2)
END DEFine

## PUBLIC: return exact source spelling, retaining quotes, escapes, numeric
## spelling and container whitespace. Absolute offsets allow chunk crossings.
## Return at most 4096 bytes; larger values report error 9 and remain accessible
## through start/length spans and json_byte%.
DEFine FuNction json_raw$(VAL jqNode%)
  LOCal jqOut$(4096),jqIndex,jqStart
  IF NOT json_valid%(jqNode%) THEN RETurn ""
  IF jsonNodes(jqNode%).length > 4096 THEN json_failat 9,jsonNodes(jqNode%).start,"Raw value exceeds 4096 bytes" : RETurn ""
  jqOut$ = "" : jqStart = jsonNodes(jqNode%).start
  FOR jqIndex = 0 TO jsonNodes(jqNode%).length-1
    jqOut$ = jqOut$ & CHR$(json_byte%(jqStart+jqIndex))
  END FOR jqIndex
  RETurn jqOut$
END DEFine

## PUBLIC: convert a validated number using QL floating-point precision/range.
## Bound source length and exponent magnitude before implicit string-to-number
## assignment; no generic VAL function is needed. jzSeen% marks e/E; accumulate
## its digits, ignoring the sign because both magnitudes share the limit.
## Reject above 128 before another multiply could overflow the signed accumulator.
## These conversion limits do not restrict valid JSON number spellings.
## Keep large seeds in real variables, not %-suffixed integers.
## Use json_raw$ for exact decimal text rather than rounded arithmetic.
DEFine FuNction json_number(VAL jzNode%)
  LOCal jzText$(128),jzIndex%,jzByte%,jzExp%,jzSeen%,jzValue
  IF NOT json_valid%(jzNode%) THEN RETurn 0
  IF jsonNodes(jzNode%).kind% <> 4 THEN json_failat 8,jsonNodes(jzNode%).start,"Number required" : RETurn 0
  IF jsonNodes(jzNode%).length > 128 THEN json_failat 9,jsonNodes(jzNode%).start,"Number conversion exceeds 128 characters" : RETurn 0
  jzText$ = json_raw$(jzNode%) : jzExp% = 0 : jzSeen% = 0
  FOR jzIndex% = 1 TO LEN(jzText$)
    jzByte% = CODE(jzText$(jzIndex%))
    IF jzSeen% AND json_digit%(jzByte%) THEN
      jzExp% = jzExp%*10+jzByte%-48
      IF jzExp% > 128 THEN json_failat 9,jsonNodes(jzNode%).start,"Number exponent exceeds conversion range" : RETurn 0
    END IF
    IF jzByte% = 69 OR jzByte% = 101 THEN jzSeen% = 1
  END FOR jzIndex%
  jzValue = jzText$
  RETurn jzValue
END DEFine

## PUBLIC Boolean accessor. Return 1 for true or 0 for false, without coercing
## numbers, null or strings to a truth value. A zero result is ambiguous until
## error% is checked: legitimate false leaves error% zero; misuse sets error 8.
DEFine FuNction json_boolean%(VAL jbNode%)
  IF NOT json_valid%(jbNode%) THEN RETurn 0
  IF jsonNodes(jbNode%).kind% = 5 THEN RETurn 1
  IF jsonNodes(jbNode%).kind% = 6 THEN RETurn 0
  json_failat 8,jsonNodes(jbNode%).start,"Boolean required"
  RETurn 0
END DEFine
